# ── Dev Caddyfile ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local TLS so the PWA can be installed and tested for real.
#
# Loopback only. `bind` is required: a `localhost:8443` site address on
# its own still opens the listener on 0.0.0.0 and merely filters by Host
# header. `auto_https disable_redirects` suppresses the :80 redirect
# server, which would otherwise bind every interface. `admin off` closes
# the config API on 2019.
#
# Upstream is `bun run serve:dist` (the built dist/), not the Vite dev
# server — the service worker only exists after a build.
#
# Port 8443 avoids needing root to bind 443. Browsers install a PWA over
# a non-standard HTTPS port without complaint.
#
# Caddy generates a local CA on first run. Service workers will not
# register behind an untrusted cert, so trust it once:
#   ~/.local/share/caddy/pki/authorities/local/root.crt
{
	admin off
	local_certs
	auto_https disable_redirects
}

localhost:8443 {
	bind 127.0.0.1
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4173
}
